{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 32, :comments ["<b>And you shall not profane the holy things of the children of Israel, and you shall not die.</b> Once you do so, there is no profanation of consecrated things, for the twenty-four priestly gifts are altogether unconsecrated. Twelve are given in Jerusalem and twelve in the provinces. And what are these twelve in Jerusalem? Hatat, asham, communal Shelamim offerings, hides of consecrated animals, the showbread, the two loaves, the omer, remnants of meal offerings, the surplus log of oil of the leper, the terumah of the thanksgiving offering, the terumah of Shelamim, and the terumah of the Nazirite's ram. And what are these twelve in the provinces? The great terumah, terumat maaser, hallah, first fruits, first of the fleece, foreleg, cheeks, stomach, firstborn of a person, firstborn of a pure animal, the firstborn of a donkey, devoted property, an inherited field, and robbery of the convert. These are the twenty-four priestly gifts. <b>Completed, the order of the portion of Korah.</b>"], :book :numbers, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 18, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T15:18:35.097432075Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}